# Temporary/local-only files excluded from distribution
.work/
*.tmp
*.cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
*.log
.DS_Store

# Large intermediate files
*.parquet
*.sqlite
*.db

# Evidence that the `*.log` rule would otherwise swallow
#
# `*.log` above (and `*.log*` / `*.log` in the root .gitignore) is there to keep
# harness scratch logs out of the distribution. It also swallowed the 317 `.log`
# files under evidence/actual-runs/, and nine of those are cited by name, with a
# recorded sha256, from `logs[]`/`evidence_files[]` slots in the execution
# records FB2-VER-EXE-000008..000012 and FB2-VER-EXE-000015. A citation that names
# a file the distribution does not contain is a checkable claim that is false on a
# clean checkout: `corpus.py check` failed there with 14 `evidence_file_missing`
# findings that this working tree cannot reproduce, because the files were present.
#
# Measurement, so the decision is auditable rather than asserted:
#   317 files, 1,708,413 bytes total (1.63 MiB), all under
#   docs/artifacts/evidence/actual-runs/ (logs-strict/, -task3/, -task4/).
# That is small enough to distribute in full, so all of it is tracked and nothing
# is excluded with a rewritten citation. The corpus is the product of this
# repository; shipping its execution logs is the point, not an accident.
#
# This is a path-scoped negation, not `!*.log`, for the same reason the HTML
# negation below is path-scoped: a blanket `!*.log` would re-include every stray
# harness log anywhere under docs/artifacts/, including logs inside the excluded
# `.work/` tree. Verified with `git check-ignore -v` on a cited log, on an
# uncited scratch log under .work/ (still ignored), and on the HTML deliverable.
!evidence/**/*.log

# Deliverables that the root Sphinx rule would otherwise exclude
#
# The root .gitignore carries `*.html` at line 36 for the Sphinx build tree, and
# it is a pre-existing rule of the project, so it is left exactly as it is. It
# does, however, also exclude reports/e2e-engineering-document.html, which is the
# deliverable of the html-e2e-engineering-document sprint, and that file would
# therefore never be committed.
#
# This is a path-specific negation rather than `!*.html`. A blanket negation would
# re-include every generated HTML page under docs/artifacts/, which is the class
# of file the root rule exists to keep out: the visual-check scratch output next
# door (docs/artifacts/diagrams/*.visual-check.html) is produced by tooling and
# must stay ignored. Only the one deliverable is named.
#
# No `!reports/` or `!*/` line is needed and none is added: git cannot re-include
# a path whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, but reports/ is not excluded by any
# rule, so the single path negation is sufficient. Verified with
# `git check-ignore -v` on this file and on two controls.
!reports/e2e-engineering-document.html
